{
  "duration": 72.299,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 0.879,
      "text": "So welcome back."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.48,
      "end": 3.859,
      "text": "I hope you have gone through the theory part for this topic."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.299,
      "end": 5.92,
      "text": "Now it's time to solve some problems."
    },
    {
      "start": 6.539,
      "end": 7.259,
      "text": "Now in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.719,
      "end": 11.239,
      "text": "a runner covers a distance of four hundred meter in four minutes."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.859,
      "end": 12.719,
      "text": "What do we need to find?"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.259,
      "end": 16.6,
      "text": "We need to find the runner's speed in kilo meter per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.139,
      "end": 19.959,
      "text": "Now we know that speed is equal to distance divided by time."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.42,
      "end": 20.6,
      "text": "Here,"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.02,
      "end": 24.079,
      "text": "the distance is four hundred meter and the time is four minutes."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.579,
      "end": 24.939,
      "text": "First,"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.439,
      "end": 27.219,
      "text": "let us convert four minutes into seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.84,
      "end": 28.879,
      "text": "Four multiplied by sixty"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.34,
      "end": 30.979,
      "text": "gives us two hundred forty seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.479,
      "end": 34.659,
      "text": "So the time is two hundred forty seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.2,
      "end": 35.459,
      "text": "Done."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.159,
      "end": 37.739,
      "text": "Now putting the values in the formula,"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.319,
      "end": 42.659,
      "text": "speed is equal to four hundred divided by two hundred forty. After simplifying this,"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.079,
      "end": 44.959,
      "text": "we get five by three meters per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.439,
      "end": 48.839,
      "text": "But the question is asking for kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.34,
      "end": 50.039,
      "text": "Be careful here,"
    },
    {
      "start": 50.379,
      "end": 52.559,
      "text": "we should not leave the answer in meters per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.979,
      "end": 58.439,
      "text": "To convert meter per second into kilometer per hour, we multiply by eighteen by five."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.919,
      "end": 61.5,
      "text": "So we multiply five by three with eighteen by five."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.899,
      "end": 65.699,
      "text": "The five gets canceled, and eighteen divided by three gives us six."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.119,
      "end": 69.22,
      "text": "Hence, the runner's speed is six kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.699,
      "end": 72.299,
      "text": "So the final answer will be option C, six."
    }
  ],
